    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing on May 15, headlined by the explosive **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Kyle Tucker** (82.65). **Gunnar Henderson** remains our primary offensive engine today, benefiting from an elite matchup against Zack Littell; the combination of a favorable park and a strong SP skill metric creates an ideal environment for his power-speed profile. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** is positioned to feast against Jack Kochanowicz, whose weaker profile elevates **Kyle Tucker** to an elite-tier start. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.62) also merits attention as a high-value play; his dynamic platoon advantage against Shane Baz drives his efficiency score well above his base projection, making him a critical component of our infield production today.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup optimizer centered on **Coby Mayo** (52.87), who sits just outside our active rotation. While **Coby Mayo** provides significant pop, he was edged out by the superior plate discipline and order placement of **Josh Jung** (61.84) and **Brady House** (60.21). Both **Josh Jung** and **Brady House** carry higher safety floors, particularly with **Brady House** benefiting from favorable platoon splits against Shane Baz. Meanwhile, our stolen base targets, **Nasim Nunez** and **Jackson Merrill**, provide essential coverage against pitchers with slower deliveries, though we remain mindful of **Jackson Merrill**\u2019s slight park disadvantage today. \n\nWe are flagging a minor risk regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board; our scores assume historical batting order positions, and any unexpected drops in the order could dampen the projections for **Liam Hicks** and **Drake Baldwin**. Furthermore, while **Andy Pages** (68.56) projects well, he faces a stern test against an elite catcher\u2019s pop time (1.89s), which slightly threatens his SB upside. We are keeping **Josh Lowe** and **Nolan Schanuel** on the bench, as they currently face unfavorable platoon matchups against Blake Snell, confirming the optimizer\u2019s preference for keeping them reserved until a more advantageous set of conditions arises.",
